Menu="OtherSettings"
Title="Unraid VSOCK Sensors"
Icon="refresh"
---
<?php
$plugin = 'unraid-vsock-sensors';
$cfg = parse_plugin_cfg($plugin);
$port = htmlspecialchars($cfg['PORT'] ?? '990', ENT_QUOTES);
$hbaMode = $cfg['HBA_MODE'] ?? 'enabled';
if ($hbaMode === 'auto') {
    $hbaMode = 'enabled';
}
$hbaBackend = $cfg['HBA_BACKEND'] ?? 'auto';
$mpt3ctlInterval = $cfg['MPT3CTL_INTERVAL'] ?? '15s';
$storcliInterval = $cfg['STORCLI_INTERVAL'] ?? ($cfg['HBA_INTERVAL'] ?? '30s');

$statusOutput = [];
exec('/etc/rc.d/rc.unraid-vsock-sensors status 2>/dev/null', $statusOutput, $statusCode);
$running = $statusCode === 0;
$status = $running ? implode(' ', $statusOutput) : 'stopped';
$version = trim((string)shell_exec('/usr/local/sbin/unraid-vsock-sensors version 2>/dev/null'));
if ($version === '') {
    $version = 'unavailable';
}
?>

### Service

_(Status)_:
: <span class="<?=$running ? 'green' : 'red'?>"><?=htmlspecialchars($status, ENT_QUOTES)?></span>

_(Version)_:
: <?=htmlspecialchars($version, ENT_QUOTES)?>

<form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#command" value="/plugins/unraid-vsock-sensors/service.sh">

_(Actions)_:
: <?php if ($running): ?>
  <button type="submit" name="#arg[1]" value="stop">_(Stop)_</button>
  <button type="submit" name="#arg[1]" value="restart">_(Restart)_</button>
  <?php else: ?>
  <button type="submit" name="#arg[1]" value="start">_(Start)_</button>
  <?php endif; ?>
</form>

### Configuration

<form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#file" value="unraid-vsock-sensors/unraid-vsock-sensors.cfg">
<input type="hidden" name="#command" value="/plugins/unraid-vsock-sensors/service.sh">
<input type="hidden" name="#arg[1]" value="restart">

_(VSOCK port)_:
: <input type="number" name="PORT" value="<?=$port?>" min="1" max="4294967294" required>

> The Proxmox client and the CoolerControl plugin must use the same port.

_(HBA monitoring)_:
: <select name="HBA_MODE">
<option value="enabled" <?=$hbaMode === 'enabled' ? 'selected' : ''?>>Enabled</option>
<option value="disabled" <?=$hbaMode === 'disabled' ? 'selected' : ''?>>Disabled</option>
</select>

> Enabled reads mpt3sas controllers directly through /dev/mpt3ctl. StorCLI remains an optional fallback for other supported controllers. Disabled explicitly clears the HBA inventory when the host agent restarts.

_(HBA backend)_:
: <select name="HBA_BACKEND">
<option value="auto" <?=$hbaBackend === 'auto' ? 'selected' : ''?>>Automatic (mpt3ctl, then StorCLI)</option>
<option value="mpt3ctl" <?=$hbaBackend === 'mpt3ctl' ? 'selected' : ''?>>Native /dev/mpt3ctl</option>
<option value="storcli" <?=$hbaBackend === 'storcli' ? 'selected' : ''?>>StorCLI</option>
</select>

> Automatic prefers /dev/mpt3ctl and uses StorCLI only when no mpt3sas IOC is found. Selecting a backend explicitly disables fallback.

_(mpt3ctl refresh interval)_:
: <select name="MPT3CTL_INTERVAL">
<option value="10s" <?=$mpt3ctlInterval === '10s' ? 'selected' : ''?>>10 seconds</option>
<option value="15s" <?=$mpt3ctlInterval === '15s' ? 'selected' : ''?>>15 seconds</option>
<option value="30s" <?=$mpt3ctlInterval === '30s' ? 'selected' : ''?>>30 seconds</option>
<option value="1m" <?=$mpt3ctlInterval === '1m' ? 'selected' : ''?>>1 minute</option>
</select>

_(StorCLI refresh interval)_:
: <select name="STORCLI_INTERVAL">
<option value="30s" <?=$storcliInterval === '30s' ? 'selected' : ''?>>30 seconds</option>
<option value="1m" <?=$storcliInterval === '1m' ? 'selected' : ''?>>1 minute</option>
<option value="5m" <?=$storcliInterval === '5m' ? 'selected' : ''?>>5 minutes</option>
</select>

> Native access can be refreshed more frequently. Automatic uses the conservative StorCLI interval because it may fall back to that backend. VSOCK requests always use the cached value.

&nbsp;

: <input type="submit" name="Apply" value="_(Apply)_">
</form>
